1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:15,100
The last one is the improper way out: a student who stopped enrolling without an approved leave. Nobody types 'AWOL' by hand. The system flags the student from the official records.

2
00:00:16,399 --> 00:00:23,600
I sign in as staff.

3
00:00:25,199 --> 00:00:38,500
This is the AWOL and Residency board. It flags cases from the source records, and the line above counts the cases in each column.

4
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:53,699
I search for Maya Torres. Her card is in the AWOL column, with the date the flag started, and it says 'Waiting for: Student'. Staff cannot move it: only the student can start a return.

5
00:00:54,799 --> 00:01:17,700
The rules here are the residence limits: five years normal and seven absolute for a master's student, seven and nine for a doctorate, and time on leave counts toward residence. Each rule shows its Handbook page.

6
00:01:19,599 --> 00:01:32,399
Opening the card shows the AWOL date, where the flag came from, and the last enrolled semester. There is no button for staff yet.

7
00:01:32,599 --> 00:01:40,399
Now I sign in as Maya.

8
00:01:42,099 --> 00:01:52,700
Her Return from AWOL page shows the flag, and a note that registration stays restricted until her return is reviewed.

9
00:02:01,599 --> 00:02:10,600
She chooses her intended return semester and her last enrolled semester, and writes her intention and her reason for returning.

10
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:17,000
She checks the summary and sends it.

11
00:02:17,199 --> 00:02:28,300
Submitted. The system classifies her as within the maximum residence, and she cannot cancel it herself; she has to contact the Graduate School office.

12
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:41,800
I sign in as staff.

13
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:50,500
Back on the staff board, the card has moved by itself to Return review.

14
00:02:50,699 --> 00:02:59,600
The request shows her written intention, the residence limits, and the policy check: eligible for Dean review.

15
00:03:08,099 --> 00:03:16,200
I drag it to With the Dean and add a note.

16
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:20,200
Forwarded, and locked for staff.

17
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:26,900
The Dean decides.

18
00:03:32,099 --> 00:03:44,800
The Dean finds Maya's card in With the Dean.

19
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:56,200
The Dean drags it to Back in the program. The window explains that approval restores her standing.

20
00:03:56,400 --> 00:04:02,300
The card lands in Back in the program: she is active again.

21
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:15,700
I sign in as staff.

22
00:04:15,900 --> 00:04:25,800
On the staff side, the next owner is the Academic Coordinator, because enrollment is a separate step.

23
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:31,600
All four steps of the tracker are complete.

24
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:42,500
The Registrar list here is a list of reports, one per approved return. Staff download it and send it through the official channel.

25
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:54,800
Now I sign in as Maya.

26
00:04:55,000 --> 00:05:05,900
And Maya sees her return approved. So leave, return and AWOL all ran on the same board, the same request window and the same Registrar list.
